Load decks of sp_vdmos against ngspice-45, written by ../load.py vdmos_load.
Builds on PATH: ngspice-45 jfngv2gd3zvi5cmr9vrqfhnziipqd09n (source hfvpfb0bgw9819wkb7kzpdaasbd0hd5r, devices/vdmos),
VACASK dhxz6l3iac3r2b8n91kcz04a0j3hs4s6 (devices/spice/vdmos.va, ngspice-47-159 vadng-pre-48).
Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/families/load_run.sh vdmos_load`. i(vd) in A, |i(vd)| at 1 GHz for acg/acd.
nom is 27 C, m=1, the control of m3 (27 C, m=3) and of off (80 C, m=3); no geometry (the family has none). tcvth absent and
fc*vj under 2.5 (the second reading's laws agree there); kp given. VACASK's instance has its thermal nodes t, tc.
Regions (vgs, vds): cut (1, 10), lin (6, 0.5), sat (3, 10). abstol=1e-12 (VACASK's Newton fails in cutoff below it).
Oracles (fd.py, last lines): each nominal region's operating point moved 1e-5 V on the gate (base) and the drain
(collector, anode), whose central differences are gm and gds of the DC law, against |i(vd)| at 1 kHz; it holds where
the conductance is well above the 1 kHz capacitive current and the differences' resolution (ngspice prints 12 digits:
about 5e-11 S), so not in cutoff or reverse. And the multiplier's metamorphic relation: every m3 reading is 3 times its
nom reading within 1e-9 relative and 1e-10 absolute (the solver's gmin is not multiplied); a failing row is printed.
The model gives vto, kp, lambda, rd, rs, rg, the gate-drain capacitance law (cgdmin, cgdmax, a), cgs and the
body diode (cjo, vj, m, fc, is, n, tt).
Result: DC agrees in every region and condition (2e-4 at most, a cutoff pA at abstol 1e-12), and at m=1 AC agrees
everywhere (nom, 3e-13; both AC the derivatives of the DC law, 2e-8). At m=3 ngspice-45's AC is not three copies:
m3/nom on ngspice is 2.63 (cut acd), 2.77 (cut acg), 2.99 (lin acd), 4.13 (lin acg), 2.93 (sat acd), 8.15 (sat acg),
where VACASK's is 3 to 1e-9 and both simulators' DC is 3. So m3 and off read up to 63% apart at 1 GHz (m3_sat_acg
22.26 against 8.20). Class: ngspice-45 multiplies a VDMOS's small-signal (its capacitances) otherwise than its DC
current; the oracle is the metamorphic relation, which no deck of the other families violates.

